@flexiarg operator/ask-the-running-work-its-state
@title Ask The Running Work Its State, Expecting Failures In The Reply
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 10 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade; THEN worded 9 ways across its proposals
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-2ZZ154 turn-9jq1Aj turn-BcboOg turn-Ca1PUp turn-OlGfA3 turn-WtlmWa turn-Xtdfoh turn-g0WX7n turn-kO8wAS turn-n5EIxj; first proposed for: Work is running out of the operator's sight, on a long probe or a metered box.
@why [process-coherence/status-refresh-before-work]

! conclusion: Reply with the position (running, for how long, what is outstanding) and any failures so far.

  + IF:
    The operator asks whether it is still running.

  + HOWEVER:
    The answer must lead with outcomes, not machinery; a running job is no reason to pause the conversation.

  + THEN:
    Reply with the position (running, for how long, what is outstanding) and any failures so far.

  + BECAUSE:
    The operator's only lever on running work is timely truth.
